;; data/datascript-tx.edn — the AUTHORED copy of the BusinessNZ catalog.
;; `src/association/facts.cljc` holds the same entries inline and is held to
;; this file by test/association/facts_test.clj; `src/association_facts.kotoba`
;; is generated from this file by scripts/gen-kotoba-port.cljs. ADR-2607141700
;; (cloud-itonami-compliance-fact-federation), Wave 0.
;;
;; Every entry names the page it comes from and the verbatim span it rests on,
;; so `kbb --backend sci scripts/verify-catalog.cljk --live` can fetch the source and fail if
;; the document no longer says it. Reachability alone would not do: a URL that
;; answers 200 without the claim looks exactly like one that supports it.
;;
;; On provenance. businessnz.org.nz answers 403 to every client this workspace
;; has tried, on every URL tried -- measured 2026-07-17 and measured again
;; 2026-09-06, so this is a standing property of the host and not a bad day.
;; teara.govt.nz does the same. The association's own words are therefore cited
;; through Internet Archive captures, whose URLs carry the capture instant and
;; stay fetchable. That is a deliberate provenance, recorded as
;; :official-businessnz-org-nz-web-archive rather than smuggled in as a direct
;; read; verify-catalog.cljs rejects an entry whose URL and provenance disagree
;; about which of the two it is.
;;
;; On dates. None of these pages states when the rule it carries was adopted --
;; a membership term or a board composition is published without a date on the
;; site. Those entries therefore carry :date-unknown-because rather than a date
;; invented from the capture instant, which would be indistinguishable, in the
;; field, from a date the association actually gave. The two founding entries
;; do carry dates, because the Wikipedia article states them.
;;
;; On people. BusinessNZ publishes the names of its board members and staff.
;; This catalog records institutional facts only and never persists a personal
;; name, so no entry is read from /our-people/ and no quote spans a name --
;; even where the surrounding sentence was the most convenient one to cite.

